    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.x\n\n### Description\n\nMini.completion 'replacement string' item contains newlines\n\n### Reproduction\n\nHave tested on both: `v0.11.0-dev-1897+g47cfe901d7-Homebrew` (`brew install --HEAD neovim`)\n\nand `v0.10.4` (`brew install neovim`)\n\n```\n-- Clone latest 'mini.nvim' (requires Git CLI installed)\nvim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\nlocal mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\nlocal clone_cmd = { 'git', 'clone', '--depth=1', 'https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim', mini_path }\nvim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\nvim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n-- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\nvim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim')\nrequire('mini.deps').setup()\nrequire('mini.completion').setup()\n\nMiniDeps.add('neovim/nvim-lspconfig')\n\nlocal lspconfig = require('lspconfig')\nlspconfig.jedi_language_server.setup{}\n```\n\nWhen attempting to perform any completion via the LSP I get the following traceback:\n\n```\nError executing vim.schedule lua callback: ...o/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/completion.lua:1132: 'replacement string' item contains new\nlines\nstack traceback:\n        [C]: in function 'nvim_buf_set_lines'\n        ...o/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/completion.lua:1132: in function 'show_signature_window'\n        ...o/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/completion.lua:1110: in function 'handler'\n        ...neovim/HEAD-47cfe90_1/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp.lua:1191: in function 'handler'\n        ...HEAD-47cfe90_1/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/client.lua:679: in function ''\n        vim/_editor.lua: in function <vim/_editor.lua:0>\n```\n\nWhat's curious I think this is only happening for completions who's documentation contains certain newlines\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a5e45304-905c-4ee3-a5fc-7f2456db105b",
